  "estimatedMinutes": 1,
  "statement": "A truck travels \\(\\dfrac{b}{6}\\) feet every \\(t\\) seconds. There are \\(3\\) feet in a yard. How many yards does the truck travel in \\(3\\) minutes?",
  "answerChoices": [
    {
      "label": "A",
      "text": "\\( \\dfrac{b}{1080t} \\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "B",
      "text": "\\( \\dfrac{30t}{b} \\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "C",
      "text": "\\( \\dfrac{30b}{t} \\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "D",
      "text": "\\( \\dfrac{10t}{b} \\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "E",
      "text": "\\( \\dfrac{10b}{t} \\)"
    }
  ],
  "answer": {
    "letter": "e",
    "value": null
  },
  "solutions": [
    {
      "id": "sol.amc-10b-2014-p8.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "This means it travels \\(\\dfrac{b}{18}\\) yards in \\(t\\) seconds since a yard is \\(3\\) feet. Then, in one second, it travels \\(\\dfrac{b}{18t}\\) yards.\n\nTherefore, in \\(3\\) minutes which is \\(180\\) seconds, it travels \\[\\dfrac{b}{18t}\\cdot 180 = \\dfrac {10b}t.\\]\n\nThus, the correct answer is E .",
      "hints": [
        "Convert feet to yards before scaling the time",
        "Three minutes is \\(180\\) seconds"
      ],
      "images": []
    }
  ],
